💭 Assistant: Now I understand what needs to be implemented. Let me analyze the requirements:

1. Implement `migrate(conn)` function in db.py
2. The function should upgrade from version 1 to version 2 database
3. Add a nullable TEXT column `email_domain` to `users` table
4. Backfill it with the lower-cased part of `email` after its last `@` (NULL when email is NULL or contains no `@`)
5. Set the single row in `schema_version` to 2
6. Must be idempotent (running on v2 database should do nothing)
7. Must not lose or alter any other data
8. Must leave exactly one row in `schema_version`

Let me implement the migrate function:



⚡ Tool Call: edit_file {"path":"db.py","old_content":"def migrate(conn):\n    raise NotImplementedError","new_content":"def migrate(conn):\n    # Check current version\n    current_version = version(conn)\n    \n    # If already at version 2, do nothing (idempotent)\n    if current_version == 2:\n        return\n    \n    # Only migrate from version 1\n    if current_version != 1:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Cannot migrate from version {current_version}\")\n    \n    # Add the new email_domain column to users table\n    try:\n        conn.execute(\"ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN email_domain TEXT\")\n    except sqlite3.OperationalError:\n        # Column already exists, which means we're already at version 2\n        # This handles the idempotent case\n        pass\n    \n    # Backfill the email_domain column with the domain part of email\n    # Extract domain part after last '@' and convert to lowercase\n    # If email is NULL or has no '@', set email_domain to NULL\n    conn.execute(\"\"\"\n        UPDATE users \n        SET email_domain = CASE \n            WHEN email IS NULL OR email NOT LIKE '%@%' THEN NULL\n            ELSE LOWER(SUBSTR(email, INSTR(email, '@') + 1))\n        END\n    \"\"\")\n    \n    # Update schema version to 2\n    conn.execute(\"UPDATE schema_version SET version = 2\")\n    conn.commit()"}
